.TH SE 1 "2025" "se 3.8.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
se \- universal package manager wrapper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B se
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIPACKAGE\fR...]
.PP
.B se
.BR \-B ", " \-\-brew
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIPACKAGE\fR...]
.PP
.B se
.BR \-M ", " \-\-make
[\fISUBCOMMAND\fR]
.PP
.B se
.BR \-C ", " \-\-cargo
\fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fICRATE\fR]
.PP
.B se
.BR \-GC ", " \-\-git\-clone
\fIURL\fR
.PP
.B se
.BR \-W ", " \-\-wget
\fIURL\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B se
is a unified package manager wrapper for Linux. It lets you install, update,
remove, and manage packages using the same commands regardless of which distro
or package manager you are running.
.PP
Supported backends: apt, nala, pacman, dnf, zypper, emerge, xbps.
.PP
The
.B \-B
/
.B \-\-brew
flag overrides the configured backend and routes the command directly to
Homebrew. This is useful on systems where both a native package manager and
Homebrew are available and you want to target Homebrew explicitly.
.PP
The
.B \-M
/
.B \-\-make
flag runs make targets in the current directory and is completely independent
of the configured package manager. A
.I Makefile
must be present in the current directory.
.PP
The
.B \-C
/
.B \-\-cargo
flag runs Cargo commands. It requires a subcommand and is independent of the
configured package manager. Note that inside this context,
.B \-B
means
.I --build
and
.B \-I
means
.IR --install ,
which are scoped to cargo and do not conflict with the top-level
.B \-B
or
.B \-I
flags.
.PP
.B \-GC
/
.B \-\-git\-clone
clones a remote git repository to the current directory.
.PP
.B \-W
/
.B \-\-wget
downloads a file from a URL using wget.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR \-B ", " \-\-brew " \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIpackage\fR]"
Use Homebrew for the following command instead of the configured package
manager. Must be placed before the command flag.
.RS
.PP
.I Examples:
.nf
se -B -S wget
se -B -I ripgrep
se -B -Up
.fi
.RE
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-make " [\fISUBCOMMAND\fR]"
Run a make target in the current directory. With no subcommand, runs plain
.BR make .
.RS
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-clean
Run
.BR "make clean" .
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-install
Run
.BR "sudo make install" .
.TP
.BR \-U ", " \-\-uninstall
Run
.BR "sudo make uninstall" .
.PP
.I Examples:
.nf
se -M
se -M -C
se -M -I
se -M -U
.fi
.RE
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-cargo " \fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fIcrate\fR]"
Run a Cargo command. Requires a subcommand.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-B ", " \-\-build
Run
.BR "cargo build --release" .
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-install " \fIcrate\fR"
Run
.BR "cargo install" " <crate>."
.PP
.I Examples:
.nf
se -C -B
se -C -I ripgrep
.fi
.RE
.TP
.BR \-GC ", " \-\-git\-clone " \fIURL\fR"
Clone the git repository at
.I URL
into the current directory.
.RS
.PP
.I Example:
.nf
se -GC https://github.com/user/repo
.fi
.RE
.TP
.BR \-W ", " \-\-wget " \fIURL\fR"
Download a file from
.I URL
using wget.
.RS
.PP
.I Example:
.nf
se -W https://example.com/file.tar.gz
.fi
.RE
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-get " \fIpackage\fR"
Install a package.
.TP
.BR \-Rm ", " \-\-remove " \fIpackage\fR"
Remove a package.
.TP
.BR \-Cl ", " \-\-purge " \fIpackage\fR"
Purge a package and its configuration files. When used with
.BR \-B ,
runs
.B brew uninstall \-\-zap
which also removes all associated cask artifacts and cached files.
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-index " \fIpackage\fR"
Search for a package in the repository.
.TP
.BR \-Up ", " \-\-update
Update the package lists.
.TP
.BR \-Ut ", " \-\-upgrade
Upgrade all installed packages.
.TP
.BR \-Rec ", " \-\-reconfigure
Detect and reconfigure the package manager. Useful if you switch distros or
want to change the backend (e.g. switch from apt to nala).
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the installed version of se.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-help
Show a short command reference.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/se/config.se
Stores the detected package manager. Delete this file or run
.B se \-\-reconfigure
to re-detect.
.SH EXAMPLES
Install a package:
.PP
.RS
.nf
se --get firefox
.fi
.RE
.PP
Install a package via Homebrew:
.PP
.RS
.nf
se --brew --get firefox
.fi
.RE
.PP
Remove a package:
.PP
.RS
.nf
se --remove firefox
.fi
.RE
.PP
Purge a package via Homebrew (removes all associated files):
.PP
.RS
.nf
se -B -Cl wget
.fi
.RE
.PP
Update and upgrade:
.PP
.RS
.nf
se --update
se --upgrade
.fi
.RE
.PP
Update and upgrade via Homebrew:
.PP
.RS
.nf
se -B --update
se -B --upgrade
.fi
.RE
.PP
Search for a package:
.PP
.RS
.nf
se --index neovim
.fi
.RE
.PP
Build and install from source using make:
.PP
.RS
.nf
se -M
se -M -I
.fi
.RE
.PP
Clean build artifacts and uninstall via make:
.PP
.RS
.nf
se -M -C
se -M -U
.fi
.RE
.PP
Build a Rust project and install a crate:
.PP
.RS
.nf
se -C -B
se -C -I ripgrep
.fi
.RE
.PP
Clone a repository and download a file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
se -GC https://github.com/user/repo
se -W https://example.com/file.tar.gz
.fi
.RE
.SH AUTHOR
Barry C <https://github.com/barryC12>
